                      operated by you or on your behalf, together with
                      every copy operated by your affiliates.

                      A "Worker or GPU Instance" is any physical machine,
                      virtual machine, microVM, container or sandbox that
                      runs the worker component of the Licensed Work,
                      processes its jobs (including parser and OCR
                      sandboxes), or provides GPU acceleration to it,
                      including GPU model inference that you host. Model
                      inference bought per request from a third-party API
                      is not a Worker or GPU Instance.

                      "vCPUs" are the logical CPUs available to each
                      Worker or GPU Instance (its CPU quota, if lower),
                      added up across the Deployment and measured at the
                      busiest moment.

